gomad: keep one copy of each prepared target per artifact store
- artifact.Store takes a target pool from its caller and makes each
  artifact's target a hard link to the pool entry sha256-<hex>
- the entry is published with a no-replace rename and verified through
  the new link, so concurrent publishers end with one entry
- a store whose filesystem cannot link publishes a private copy and the
  result says unshared; any other link failure fails the publication
- the artifact reader opens the manifest's target without the
  single-link check and keeps that check for every other payload
- campaign, exploration-round, corpus, and minimizer stores pass the
  pool of their owner: the artifacts root, the corpus, the output root
- the sharing form and its reasons are recorded in the spec

